1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,325
You fill a notebook with handwriting,

2
00:00:02,325 --> 00:00:03,675
then your iPad breaks.

3
00:00:03,675 --> 00:00:05,025
The notes are gone.

4
00:00:05,025 --> 00:00:07,388
Your notes should live in your account,

5
00:00:07,388 --> 00:00:08,738
not on one device.

6
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:13,271
DevPad is a notebook backend that saves typed and

7
00:00:13,271 --> 00:00:16,048
handwritten notes to each signed-in user's account.

8
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:19,333
This is DevPad's API running locally.

9
00:00:19,333 --> 00:00:23,609
Folders, notebooks, pages, cells and strokes each get their own endpoints.

10
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,301
Create Notebook takes a title,

11
00:00:26,301 --> 00:00:28,202
folder, cover color and template.

12
00:00:28,202 --> 00:00:29,723
Pages then hold code,

13
00:00:29,723 --> 00:00:31,244
text or ink cells.

14
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,541
Try it out makes the form live,

15
00:00:33,541 --> 00:00:35,082
so we can send a real request.

16
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,911
Execute sends it to the running server,

17
00:00:37,911 --> 00:00:39,118
with no sign-in token.

18
00:00:39,900 --> 00:00:41,970
The server answers 401,

19
00:00:41,970 --> 00:00:46,111
not authenticated. Notebooks belong to a signed-in user:

20
00:00:46,111 --> 00:00:48,181
no token, no data.

21
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:52,838
The iPad app is written in Swift and signs

22
00:00:52,838 --> 00:00:56,776
in through Supabase. It sends tokens to a FastAPI

23
00:00:56,776 --> 00:01:01,151
backend, which stores data with SQLAlchemy in SQLite or Postgres.

24
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:05,648
Next: typed-note editing and free placement of cells,

25
00:01:05,648 --> 00:01:07,372
then images and attachments,

26
00:01:07,372 --> 00:01:09,096
search and offline sync.

27
00:01:10,100 --> 00:01:13,940
Try it at github.com/yuchan-chung1964/DevPad
